-- title:
--   Original finite-activity stopped cash: dominated, conditionally centred intrinsic two-noise mesh decomposition
-- statement:
--   For the literal spectrally negative Lévy source, same probability space and filtration, and actual admissible dividend payments stopped at the bounded right-continuous random clock, construct intrinsic Gaussian and compensated-negative-jump mesh martingale approximations. Each sequence must be integrable and initially conditionally centred, dominated by an integrable envelope, and converge almost surely to a limiting noise; the remainder must vanish almost surely. On each mesh, the full original discounted terminal reserve plus cash is bounded by w(x) plus both original-noise approximations and remainder. No auxiliary independent process or assumed reward inequality is permitted. This yields the exact original stopped-cash conditional HJB bound via Proved JB24 dominated two-channel transfer.
-- source:
--   Original cash-ledger obligation B215; Proved avram_jb24_finite_mesh_stopped_cash_condexp_upper; original stopped Itô-Meyer finite activity source.

